        "name": "Debanjan Maji",
        "email": "debanjanmaji700@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-14T12:58:21Z"
      },
      "message": "fix: use valid Python and Ruby versions in mise config\n\nThe .mise.toml file specified Python 3.14.3 and Ruby 3.4.8, which don't exist yet. Python 3.14 and Ruby 3.4 are not released as of February 2026.\n\nThis was causing all CI build-container jobs to fail when mise tried to install these non-existent versions.\n\nFixed by:\n\n- Changing Python from 3.14.3 to 3.12.8 (stable, meets pyproject.toml >=3.12)\n\n- Changing Ruby from 3.4.8 to 3.3.6 (latest stable, compatible with Gemfile ~>3.2)\n\n- Bumping container tag to force rebuild\n\nFixes widespread CI failures affecting all recent PRs.",
      "tree": {
